  "metaDescription": "Search operations are underway for missing employees following a fatal factory fire at PT Fonusa Agung Mulia in the Cikande industrial area of Serang.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Search and rescue efforts continue for approximately 50 employees reported missing following a blaze at the candy manufacturing facility.",
    "Banten regional police are conducting DNA testing on seven recovered remains to facilitate identification due to the state of the bodies.",
    "Management at PT Fonusa Agung Mulia has expressed condolences to the families of victims and pledged cooperation with the ongoing investigation."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A significant fire occurred at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory, located in the Pancatama Industrial Estate in Cikande, Serang, Indonesia. The incident, which began on Saturday afternoon, has led to a major search operation for employees reported missing. Authorities have confirmed the recovery of seven body bags from the site, though identification remains difficult due to the condition of the remains, prompting Banten police to utilize DNA testing. Company representatives, including CEO Steven Erwin Wijaya, have formally apologized for the incident and stated that the facility adhered to established safety and occupational health standards. As the investigation into the cause of the fire proceeds, the company has committed to providing support to the affected employees and their families during this period of mourning.",
